  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Chef Barinov stops the wedding officiant from leaving and turns to Elena Pavlovna. Explaining that his two months in a coma taught him to cherish every single moment, he asks Elena to marry him right there—and she says yes!",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "До свидания, хотя подождите минуту.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Лена, может, мы сейчас поженимся?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Витя, имей хоть немного совести.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Твоя дочь сбежала из-под венца.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она вспомнит это с улыбкой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она молодая и сильная женщина.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А я уже не молодой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надо беречь каждую нашу минуту.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И наслаждаться каждым новым мгновением.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давай будем как муж и жена.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Скажи, ты согласна или нет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Объявляю вас мужем и женой!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "До свидания, хотя подождите минуту.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Goodbye, although wait a minute.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'until', while 'a minute' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Лена, может, мы сейчас поженимся?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Lena, maybe we should get married right now?' Notice how Russian expresses 'Lena' and 'we will get married' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Elena answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Витя, имей хоть немного совести.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vitya, have at least a little conscience.' The meaning hinges on 'have' working together with 'conscience' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Твоя дочь сбежала из-под венца.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Your daughter just ran away from the altar.' Notice how Russian expresses 'your' and 'wedding altar' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она вспомнит это с улыбкой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She will remember this with a smile.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'she' and finishing on 'smile'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она молодая и сильная женщина.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She is a young and strong woman.' Notice how Russian expresses 'she' and 'woman' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А я уже не молодой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I am no longer young.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'and' before landing on 'young'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надо беречь каждую нашу минуту.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We must treasure every minute of ours.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'need' and 'to treasure' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И наслаждаться каждым новым мгновением.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And savor every new moment.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'and' and 'to enjoy' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давай будем как муж и жена.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let us be together as husband and wife.' The grammar packs 'come on' and 'wife' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Скажи, ты согласна или нет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Tell me, do you agree or not?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'say' before landing on 'no'. Elena answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Объявляю вас мужем и женой!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I pronounce you husband and wife!' Notice how Russian expresses 'I declare' and 'wife' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
